{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1267591-question-about-a-texas-relic","id":1267591,"title":"question about a Texas Relic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-15T09:20:32-08:00","id":1267591,"title":"question about a Texas Relic","content":"watching King of the Hill reminded me of something.<br /> <img src=\"https://guidelive.imgix.net/1508428628-2012-Big-Tex-Burns.jpg?fit=crop&amp;crop=faces,top,right&amp;q=50&amp;w=400&amp;h=300\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <br /> so this happened a few years back- Big Tex, the mascot of the Texas State fair caught fire and burned to his metal frame. my question is this- what sort of fun stuff happens in the ShadowLands because of this? what can the wraiths of Dallas do with a 55 foot tall cowboy statue? does somebody go stompy with a giant? did the specters get a siege weapon? are the words &quot;HOWDY FOLKS WELCOME TO THE STATE FAIR OF TEXAS&quot; echoing through the lands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T14:07:21-08:00","id":1269349,"title":"","content":"Source of Pathos, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T21:06:53-08:00","id":1269434,"title":"","content":"True Story: Big Texas was once a giant statue of Santa at a Christmas theme park. That is why his left arm is positioned like that, he was holding a bag of toys. So, maybe when it appears in the Shadowlands, it's as this giant Santa. Or a combo of Santa and cowboy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T21:44:40-08:00","id":1269750,"title":"","content":"Man this is why I want Wraith to have more then just human ghosts in the Underworld. I know we have Plasmics as a ex misc group but we need freedom to have giant flaming Cowboys in our Necropoli!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Post